	(text "DESIGN VALUES (LAN8670 DS60001573K; OPEN Alliance 10BASE-T1S; Node60 DEC-007, DEC-012)\nMode straps MODE[1:0] = 10b (RMII, 50 MHz REFCLKIN): RXD3/MODE1 pulled up, RXD2/MODE0 pulled down, 10k each.\nPHYAD[4:0] = 00001b: RXER/PHYAD0 up; CRSDV/PHYAD1, RXD0/PHYAD2, RXD1/PHYAD3, CRS/PHYAD4 down (10k).\n  PHYAD is a hardware strap only; the PLCA node ID is commissioned in flash (separate from PHYAD).\nTXEN 10k pull-down (Microchip: prevents transmission while the MAC is in reset). MDIO 10k pull-up to VDDP.\nIRQ_N open drain, 10k pull-up to 3V3_MAIN -> T1S_IRQ_L to the MCU (PHY ready after cold boot).\nINH: P-channel open drain to VDDAU with 10k pull-down (Microchip ref.), drives the 3V3_MAIN buck EN and the\n  LM74910H SLEEP pin directly (DEC-004). No FS26, latch or MCU gate.\nRESET_N on RESET_L (TPS3702 window supervisor + S32K344 RESET_B): every MCU reset also resets the PHY,\n  so straps are re-latched and firmware always re-initializes from a known state.\nWAKE_IN unused (no local wake, DEC-007) -> VSS per datasheet. TXD2/TXD3 unused in RMII (internal pull-downs).\nTXER/ACMA unused -> VSS. TXCLK/RXPI, COL, RXCLK/WAKE_OUT, GPIO0, XTO unused: no-connect.\nRBIAS 12.4k 1 % (Microchip reference).\nDecoupling: 10nF + 100nF at every VDDP/VDDA/VDDAU pin, 10uF bulk on VDDP and VDDA (Microchip sec. 6).\n  10nF goes closest to its pin. Ferrite beads in the reference are optional and not fitted.\nLine interface (DEC-012 rev. B, Microchip AN1718), layout order connector -> ESD -> termination -> DC block -> CMC -> PHY:\n  C DC block 2 x 100nF C0G 100 V (OPEN Alliance: >= 50 V). FL501 ACT1210E-241 (240 uH, 10BASE-T1S rated).\n  D ESD 2 x VETH100A1DD1 (<= 2 pF/line) right at the connector. Keep the pair symmetric through the CMC.\n  Capacitance budget: CMDI <= 25 pF: transceiver 10 + CMC 10 + ESD 1 (pair) leaves ~4 pF for connector + traces.\n  Termination: OA split network switched by latching relay K501 (DEC-017), box below right.\n50 MHz clock: Y501 ECS-3225SMVQ, enable tied high (runs with 3V3_MAIN). One output, two 33R series resistors,\n  one to PHY XTI/REFCLKIN, one to the MCU RMII REF_CLK. Length-match both traces (Microchip layout note).\nOPEN: TDK has not published a CMC class for ACT1210E-241 (DEC-012 risk). VETH100A1DD1 24 V working voltage\n  vs a 24 V short to battery on the bus: see DEC-012.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
